# Lines GRVER's test (grver.bat) must write to COM1 on GR-DOS
# (scripts/smoke-test): the kernel's version, from VERSION; the help and
# the exit statuses; and each of FAKEID's imitations (fakeid.asm). GRVER
# takes none of them for GR-DOS but G, a valid answer.

^GRDOS-TEST-BEGIN$
^== GRVER$
^GR-DOS \d+\.\d\d$
^EXIT 0$
^== GRVER \/\?$
^Displays the GR-DOS release version, as the GR-DOS kernel reports it\.$
^GRVER \[\/\?\]$
^Exit status: 0 GR-DOS, 1 not GR-DOS, 2 invalid response, 3 bad parameter\.$
^EXIT 0$
^== GRVER \/X$
^Invalid parameter - \/X$
^Displays the GR-DOS release version, as the GR-DOS kernel reports it\.$
^GRVER \[\/\?\]$
^Exit status: 0 GR-DOS, 1 not GR-DOS, 2 invalid response, 3 bad parameter\.$
^EXIT 3$
^== GRVER A B$
^Invalid parameter - A$
^Displays the GR-DOS release version, as the GR-DOS kernel reports it\.$
^GRVER \[\/\?\]$
^Exit status: 0 GR-DOS, 1 not GR-DOS, 2 invalid response, 3 bad parameter\.$
^EXIT 3$
^== FAKEID U$
^GR-DOS kernel not detected\.$
^EXIT 1$
^== FAKEID D$
^GR-DOS kernel not detected\.$
^EXIT 1$
^== FAKEID S$
^GR-DOS kernel response not valid\.$
^EXIT 2$
^== FAKEID C$
^GR-DOS kernel response not valid\.$
^EXIT 2$
^== FAKEID M$
^GR-DOS kernel response not valid\.$
^EXIT 2$
^== FAKEID R$
^GR-DOS kernel response not valid\.$
^EXIT 2$
^== FAKEID G$
^GR-DOS 2\.99$
^EXIT 0$
^GRDOS-TEST-END$
